  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating Sustainable and Clean Energy Access Transformation in Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Program Development Objective (PDO) is to increase access to clean energy in rural and peri-urban areas of Zambia.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of the Accelerating Sustainable and Clean Energy Access Transformation (ASCENT) in Zambia Project is to increase access to clean energy in rural and peri-urban areas of Zambia. The Theory of Change for the Program is a sub-set of the ASCENT MPA&apos;s overall program framework. The program&apos;s activities described in next section are fully aligned with the scope of activities under the ASCENT MPA, drawing on ASCENT&apos;s menu of options under all of its three pillars: (i) Pillar 1: Regional and National Platforms to accelerate energy access (Result Area (RA) 3), (ii) Pillar 2: Expanding grid electrification (RA 2); and (iii) Pillar 3: Scaling up DRE and Clean Cooking (RA 1). Result Area 1: Increasing Supply of Distributed Renewable Energy,  focuses on supporting the provision of clean energy in rural and peri-urban areas through renewable energy mini grids, solar standalone systems and efficient and clean cooking solutions. Result Area 2: Expanding On-Grid Access to Electricity, supports grid intensification, densification and last-mile connections under the REP to provide financing for on-grid connections in rural areas using the approaches under the RBF Subsidy Program. Result Area 3: Strengthening National Platform for Energy Access, will support strengthening the policy framework for DRE solutions and the capacity of sector institutions in expanding on-grid and DRE solutions.</narrative>
  </description>
